# firmware.ti59 Keystrokes to enable firmware listing
#
# In early 1980 a personal letter from Maurice Swinnen, the editor of TI PPC Notes, explained that the TI-59 firmware could be
# observed by performing the following unusual keyboard sequence while disregarding the flashing displays:
# Step              Display
# Turnon            0
# 2nd-0p-09         Flashing 0.
# 2nd-Pgm-24        Flashing 0.
# R/S               Flashing 0
# R/S               Flashing 1
# R/S               Flashing 00
# 9-2nd-Op-17       Flashing 239.89
# GTO-0             Flashing 239.89
# R/S               Flashing 0. 00
# 2nd-DMS           Flashing 0
# LRN               000 82
#
# Initially this did not work on the ewmulator. Problem was in LIB.PC.IN (opcode 0A2E): Reading the ROM PC was destructive.

# These are the above keystrokes
KEYSTROKES:
21  2nd
64  9
64  9
21  2nd
31  LRN
83  2
72  4
91  R/S
Wait: 5s
91  R/S
Wait: 5s
91  R/S
Wait: 5s
64  9
21  2nd
64  9
82  1
62  7
61  GTO
92  0
91  R/S
Wait: 1s
21  2nd
83  2
Wait: 2s
31 LRN
